      "question": {
        ":question/id": "1587c689-cbee-55f7-a0e2-34ec93788581",
        ":question/problem": "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${f}^{\u2032}(x)-4x=1$ that satisfies the condition $f(1)=-1.$",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "a650a374-67c6-5e21-99f8-83f75be32e85",
            ":answer-field/key": "selection",
            ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
            ":answer-field/choices": [
              {
                ":answer/id": "7d9fdcda-342c-50cb-97f2-a2f8e6b2919e",
                ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
                ":answer/value": "f(x)=x^{2} + 2 x - 4"
              },
              {
                ":answer/id": "49ac4877-aee0-59d8-9205-d57b8fd1b613",
                ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
                ":answer/value": "f(x)=x^{2} - 2 x"
              },
              {
                ":answer/id": "42c54f9c-dfb4-5160-875b-f162bbdac971",
                ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
                ":answer/value": "f(x)=2 x^{2} + x - 4"
              },
              {
                ":answer/id": "812f59d5-1a56-53e1-b47e-540189872719",
                ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
                ":answer/value": "f(x)=2 x^{2} + x - 1"
              },
              {
                ":answer/id": "2899fa1a-d971-5ad5-a894-a0d0f94c3cfd",
                ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
                ":answer/value": "f(x)=2 x^{2} + 3 x - 6"
              }
            ],
            ":answer-field/correct": [
              ":answer/id",
              "42c54f9c-dfb4-5160-875b-f162bbdac971"
            ]
          }
        ],
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n{f}^{\u2032}(x)=4x+1.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{\u2032}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (4x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =4\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =4(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2})+x+C \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}+x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $f(x)=2{x}^{2}+x+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $f(1)=-1$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & =2(1)^{2}+1+C \\\\ -1 & =2+1+C \\\\ C & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\nf(x)=2{x}^{2}+x-4.\n$$"
