      "question": {
        ":question/id": "39ca7e64-b047-5f43-a11d-75fa543a2983",
        ":question/problem": "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $8x-\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={x}^{2}$ that satisfies the condition $y(2)=5.$\n\n$y=-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}\\,+${{field-1}}",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "77658474-f410-5274-9335-ad36bd10fcf1",
            ":answer-field/key": "field-1",
            ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/blank",
            ":answer-field/choices": [
              {
                ":answer/id": "6976ac7b-e1df-57f8-9019-43b52904bf57",
                ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
                ":answer/value": "4 x^{2} - \\frac{25}{3}"
              }
            ],
            ":answer-field/correct": [
              ":answer/id",
              "6976ac7b-e1df-57f8-9019-43b52904bf57"
            ]
          }
        ],
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-{x}^{2}+8x.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-{x}^{2}+8x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+8\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+4{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+4{x}^{2}+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $y(2)=5$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+4{x}^{2}+C \\\\ 5 & =-\\frac{{2}^{3}}{3}+4({2}^{2})+C \\\\ 5 & =-\\frac{8}{3}+16+C \\\\ 5 & =\\frac{40}{3}+C \\\\ C & =-\\frac{25}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is \n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+4{x}^{2}-\\frac{25}{3}.\n$$"
      },
